# The classic hello world: display a greeting string.
#
# `disp` prints any value; given a string it prints the text as-is.
# (The APL-style one-liner is just the bare expression `"Hello, world!"`,
# whose result the REPL prints -- `disp` makes the intent explicit.)
#
# Runs both interpreted and compiled to a native binary -- `disp` and
# strings are supported on the compile path, so both print the same
# text:
#
#   examples/scripts/run.sh examples/hello-world.mlpl            # interpret
#   examples/scripts/run.sh --native examples/hello-world.mlpl  # compile + run

disp("Hello, world!")
